  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Health Sector preparedness and response to the cholera outbreak in affected woredas in Somali and Oromia regions.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to provide health assistance to people affected by cholera in Somali and Oromia regions. This WHO project provides health services. The project provides humanitarian assistance to 205,836 people, including 50,385 women, 48,414 men, 107,037 children, and including 36,236 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
